Hello, I would like to make a mortgage calculator for my clients.
Please ask the client for the price of the house, then ask how much deposit they are putting down, then ask for the yearly interest rate in percent, and finally ask for how many years the loan will last.
The loan amount is the house price minus the deposit. Please show the loan amount.
To get the monthly payment, take the yearly interest rate, divide it by 100 and then by 12 to get the monthly rate. The number of months is the number of years times 12. The monthly payment is the loan times the monthly rate, divided by (1 minus (1 plus the monthly rate) to the power of minus the number of months).
Please show the monthly payment rounded to the cent.
Finally, please show the total amount paid over the whole loan, which is the monthly payment times the number of months.
Thank you!
